text	The letter and the open issues agree on one point and conflict on one. One point in the letter has no issue of its own. I changed nothing.  **1. Who gets a new partner rate: #12 conflicts with the letter.** - **Letter:** a new rate applies only to customers the partner brings after the change. Current customers keep their commissions. The letter gives no option. - **#12:** the merchant chooses in a dialog. The default is **All customers**, which is the opposite of what the client wants. The test in #12 ("keeps the default → the 3 customers pay 7%") checks for that opposite result. - **#12 is out of date:** it was decided on 29 Oct and says the client "no longer has to answer our question 1." The client answered on 30 Oct.  **2. Payouts: no conflict.** The letter says payouts stay monthly, on the 5th. #13 says the same.  **3. Rate history: only partly covered.** The client wants every change of a partner's rate in the partner's history. #12 says only that the history records the dialog choice. No issue asks to log every rate change. If you drop the dialog from #12, nothing covers this point.  The letter does not mention #14 (CSV export).  **You need to decide** whether #12 stays as a dialog or becomes "new customers only." If you keep the dialog, I suggest at least making "New customers only" the default. Tell me which one and I will: - rewrite #12 to match, including its title and acceptance test, - correct the 29 Oct reasoning, - file a separate issue for the rate-change history.
