text	#12 is assigned to rivera, so it is busy. Per the rules it gets a one-line comment only. Its body stays unchanged.
Bash	gh issue comment 12 --body 'Decided on 6 Nov 2026, after the client letter of 30 Oct (docs/letters/2026-10-30-client.md): the default of the dialog is now **New customers only**; **All customers** stays as a choice. The body and its acceptance test (which keep "All customers" as the default) are out of date on this point.'
text	Here is the paragraph for the reply:  > **Change of a partner's rate.** Thank you for your answer. When you change the rate of a partner, the new rate applies by default only to customers that the partner brings after the change. The commissions on current customers stay as they are. For the cases where you want the new rate for everyone, the same dialog also lets you choose "All customers". Then the new rate applies to every current customer of the partner, starting from their next payment. The partner's history records each rate change and which of the two options you chose.  The last sentence also answers their point 3 (rate history). Remove it if point 3 has its own paragraph in your reply.  **On the tracker:** I left a comment on #12 about the new default ("New customers only"), with the date and a link to the letter: https://github.com/acme/shop/issues/12#issuecomment-1. I did not edit the body of #12, because the issue is assigned to rivera. So its body and acceptance test still say "All customers" is the default. Rivera or you should update them. I can do it if you tell me rivera agrees.
